data: {"type":"response.function_call_arguments.done","sequence_number":302,"item_id":"fc_02f8293d92061092016adb4a3ffb18819186eda3dcac502d7c","output_index":2,"arguments":"{\"obstacle_json\":\"{\\\"status\\\":\\\"TASK_INCOMPLETE\\\",\\\"location\\\":\\\"H004 and exact L(K)-action on M ⊗_ℤ K\\\",\\\"explanation\\\":\\\"Continued formalization probes. A source-facing candidate data structure for a rank-(lambda+1) free lattice inside a complex vector space, including its complex basis, lattice inclusion, highest vector, and divided-power preservation, type-checks after making the divided-power definition noncomputable. An exact `TensorProduct ℤ M K` type also type-checks when module instances are explicit. The action of the source Chevalley generators on that tensor product and a complete faithful H004 proposition are not yet wired into the interface. I therefore cannot honestly submit the requested final artifact yet.\\\",\\\"basis\\\":\\\"Actual check_lean_types pass for `LatticeData n` as specified in the immediately preceding probe; actual pass for `TensorProduct ℤ M K` and its K-module instance when M's instances are explicit. NL0 H004/S004 define the induced action and arbitrary admissible lattice; S001-S008 prescribe the proof route. No implication has been judged false or unsupported.\\\",\\\"partial_progress\\\":\\\"Updated findings: use Module.Basis, not Basis; divided powers over ℂ require a noncomputable definition; avoid bundled instance projection issue by keeping M and its ℤ-module instances explicit parameters. The entire task packet and relevant Yui rules were previously read. No artifact submitted or accepted.\\\"}\"}"}

